#, no-c-format
msgid "Frogs Drive 5, London"
msgstr "Frogs Drive 5, London"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1505
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Such a table can be made both in a spreadsheet and in a database. Using a "
"spreadsheet is very easy, of course. What problems do we encounter at this "
"stage?"
msgstr ""
"Ovakva tabela se može napraviti koristeći tabelarno prikazivanje ili u bazi "
"podataka. Korištenje tabelarnog prikaza je naravno, veoma jednostavno. S "
"kojim problemima se susrećemo sada?"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1508
#, no-c-format
msgid "Referential data integrity"
msgstr "Referencijalni integritet podataka"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1509
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Suppose you are using a spreadsheet and you need to change the address of at "
"least one person. You have a small problem: you often have to change the "
"address in many rows. For example, Joan takes three rows. A real problem "
"will arise if you forget to change one of the rows - the address assigned to "
"this person will be ambiguous, hence your data loses integrity."
msgstr ""
"Zamislite da koristite tabelarni prikaz i da želite promijeniti adresu "
"stanovanja barem jedne osobe. Imate mali problem: često trebate promijeniti "
"adresu u više redova. Npr. Joan zauzima tri reda. Pravi problem će porasti "
"ukoliko zaboravite da promijenite jedan od redova, adresa dodijeljena ovoj "
"osobi će postati dvosmislena i tako dolazi do gubitka cjelovitosti podataka."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1511
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Moreover there is no simple way of deleting a chosen person from the table "
"since you have to remember about deleting all rows related to him or her."
msgstr ""
"Čak štaviše ne postoji jednostavan način brisanja odabrane osobe iz tabele "
"jer morate zapamtiti i obrisati sve redove koji su povezani s tom osobom."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1514
#, no-c-format
msgid "Data redundancy"
msgstr "Suvišnost podataka"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1515
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is directly connected to the previous problem. In fields Name and "
"surname and Address the same data is entered many times. This is typical of "
"a spreadsheets' ineffective way of storing data because the database grows "
"unnecessarily, thus requiring more computer resources (larger size of data "
"and slower access)."
msgstr ""
"Ovo je direktno povezano sa prethodnim problemom. U poljima 'Ime i prezime' "
"i ' Adresa' isti podatak je unešen više puta. Ovo je tipičan primjer "
"neefektivnog načina rada tabelarnog prikaza jer baza podataka nepotrebno "
"raste što zahtjeva više resura računara (povećana veličina i sporiji "
"pristup)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1517
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"How can you solve these problems with a database? You can split information "
"into smaller chunks by creating an additional table <replaceable>Persons</"
"replaceable> with only two columns: <replaceable>Name and surname</"
"replaceable> and <replaceable>Address</replaceable>:"
msgstr ""
"Kako možete riješiti problem koristeći baze podataka? Možete podijeliti "
"informacije u manje dijelove kreirajući dodatnu tabelu <replaceable>Osobe</"
"replaceable>  sa samo dvije kolone: <replaceable>Ime i prezime</"
"replaceable>  i <replaceable>Adresa</replaceable> :"

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:1521 index.docbook:1568 index.docbook:1653
#, no-c-format
msgid "Persons table"
msgstr "Tabela osoba"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1549
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each row in the table <replaceable>Persons</replaceable> corresponds to a "
"single person. Table <replaceable>Contacts</replaceable> is from now on a "
"relation to the table <replaceable>Persons</replaceable>."
msgstr ""
"Svaki red u tabeli <replaceable>Osobe</replaceable> predstavlja jednu osobu. "
"Tabela <replaceable>Kontakti</replaceable> je od sada u vezi sa tabelom "
"<replaceable>Osobe</replaceable>."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1552
#, no-c-format
msgid "Data integrity and validity"
msgstr "Validnost i cjelokupnost podataka"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1553
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note the way data is entered in the fields <replaceable>Name and surname</"
"replaceable> and <replaceable>Address</replaceable>. People entering data "
"can be fallible, sometimes even negligent. In our sample data we have both "
"different sequence of entering name and surname (Joan Smith and Smith Joan; "
"Adam and ADAM) and many more ways of entering the same address. Surely you "
"can think of many other ways."
msgstr ""
"Primijetite na koji se način podaci dodaju u polja <replaceable>Ime i "
"prezime</replaceable> i <replaceable>Adresa</replaceable>. Osobe koje unose "
"podatke mogu biti nemarne. U našem primjeru imamo drukčije načine unosa "
"imena i prezimena (Joan Smith i Smith Joan; Adam i ADAM) i mnogo drugih "
"načina za unos adrese. Sigurno se možete dosjetiti još mnogo načina."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1555
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The above problem shows that &eg; when searching the telephone number of a "
"person whose address is <quote>Western Gate 1, Warsaw</quote> you will not "
"get a full result. You will get only one row instead of three. Moreover You "
"will also not find all the telephone numbers searching for the value "
"<quote>Joan Smith</quote> in the field <replaceable>Name and surname</"
"replaceable>, because <quote>Smith Joan</quote> will not fit to <quote>Joan "
"Smith</quote>."
msgstr ""
"Gore pomenuto pokazuje da &eg; kada pretražujemo broj telefona osobe čija je "
"adresa <quote>Western Gate 1, Warsaw</quote>, nećemo dobiti kompletan "
"rezultat. Dobit ćemo samo red umjesto tri. Dalje, također nećete pronaći sve "
"telefonske brojeve u pretrazi po <quote>Joan Smith</quote> u polju "
"<replaceable>Ime i prezime</replaceable> jer  <quote>Smith Joan</quote>  se "
"neće poklopiti sa <quote>Joan Smith</quote>."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1557
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"How can you solve these problems using a database? You can do this by "
"changing the design of the table <replaceable>Persons</replaceable> by:"
msgstr ""
"Na koji način možete riješiti ove probleme koristeći bazu podataka? Ovo je "
"izvodivo promjenom dizajna tabele <replaceable>Osobe</replaceable> tako što:"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1560
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Dividing data in the field <guilabel>Name and surname</guilabel> into two "
"separate fields: <replaceable>Name</replaceable> and <replaceable>Surname</"
"replaceable>."
msgstr ""
"Dijeljenjem polja <guilabel>Ime i prezime</guilabel> u dva odvojena: "
"<replaceable>Ime</replaceable> i <replaceable>Prezime</replaceable>."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1561
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Dividing data in the field <replaceable>Address</replaceable> into three "
"separate fields: <replaceable>Street</replaceable>, <replaceable>House "
"number</replaceable> and <replaceable>City</replaceable>."
msgstr ""
"Dijeljenjem podataka u polju  <replaceable>Adresa</replaceable> na tri "
"odvojena polja: <replaceable>Ulica</replaceable>, <replaceable>Kućanski "
"broj</replaceable> i <replaceable>Grad</replaceable>."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1562
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Guaranteeing data correctness: by ensuring that no fields are empty, &eg; "
"you must always enter house number."
msgstr ""
"Garantovanje ispravnosti podataka: osiguravanjem da polja nisu prazna, &eg; "
"uvijek morate unijeti kućanski broj."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1564
#, no-c-format
msgid "A modified table looks something like this:"
msgstr "Modificirana tabela izgleda ovako:"

