msgid "<para>5</para>"
msgstr "<para>5</para>"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1611 index.docbook:1700
#, no-c-format
msgid "London"
msgstr "London"

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:1616
#, no-c-format
msgid "Conditions"
msgstr "Uslovi"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1621 index.docbook:1624 index.docbook:1627 index.docbook:1630
#: index.docbook:1633
#, no-c-format
msgid "required field"
msgstr "obavezno polje"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1639
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Thanks to introducing the condition required field we can be sure that the "
"entered data is complete. In case of other tables you may of course allow "
"omitting certain fields while entering data."
msgstr ""
"Zahvaljujući uvođenju uvjeta obaveznih polja možemo biti sigurni da su "
"unešeni podaci kompletni. U slučaju drugih tabela naravno da možete "
"izostaviti određena polja pri unosu podataka."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1642
#, no-c-format
msgid "Limiting data view"
msgstr "Ograničavanje prikaza podataka"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1643
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A spreadsheet displays all rows and columns of the table which is bothersome "
"in case of very large data sheets. You may of course filter and sort rows in "
"spreadsheets, however you must be extra careful while doing so. Spreadsheet "
"users are in risk of forgetting that their data view has been filtered what "
"can lead to mistakes. For example, while calculating sums you may think you "
"have 100 rows of data while in fact there are 20 rows more hidden."
msgstr ""
"Tabelarni prikaz prikazuje sve redove i kolone tabele što je zamorno u "
"slučaju veoma velike količine podataka. Možete naravno filtrirati i "
"sortirati redove u tabelarnom prikazu, međutim morate biti veoma pažljivi. "
"Korisnici tabelarnog prikaza mogu zaboraviti da su njihovi podaci "
"isfiltrirani što može dovesti do grešaka. Na primjer, pri proračunu sume "
"možete se prevariti da imate stotinu redova podataka dok u stvari imate još "
"20 sakrivenih redova."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1645
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to work on a small subset of data, &eg; to send it for others to "
"edit, you can copy and paste it to another spreadsheet and after editing "
"paste the changed data back to the main spreadsheet. Such <quote>manual</"
"quote> editing may cause data loss or incorrect calculations."
msgstr ""
"Ukoliko radite s malom količinom podataka, &eg; šaljete nekom drugom na "
"obradu, možete kopirati i zalijepiti podatke na drugi tabelarni prikaz i "
"nakon uređivanja zalijepiti promijenjene podatke nazad u glavni tabelarni "
"prikaz. Takvo  <quote>ručno</quote> uređivanje može uzrokovati gubitak "
"podataka i netačne proračune."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1647
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To limit the data view database applications offer queries, forms and "
"reports."
msgstr ""
"Za ograničavanje prikaza podataka, aplikacije baza podataka nude upite, "
"obrasce i izvještaje."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1649
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A very practical way of limiting is the following extended version of the "
"previously described table <replaceable>Persons</replaceable>:"
msgstr ""
"Voma praktičan način ograničavanja prikaza je sljedeća proširena verzija "
"prethodno opisane tabele  <replaceable>Osobe</replaceable>:"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1662
#, no-c-format
msgid "Income"
msgstr "Prihod"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1683
#, no-c-format
msgid "2300"
msgstr "2300"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1703
#, no-c-format
msgid "1900"
msgstr "1900"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1709
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Let's assume that the newly introduced column Income contains confidential "
"data. How can you share &eg; contact details of the persons with your "
"coworkers but without revealing their income? It is possible if you share "
"only a query and not the whole table. The query could select all columns "
"except for the column Income. In database world such a query is often known "
"as a view."
msgstr ""
"Pretpostavimo da upravo opisana kolona Prihoda sadrži povjerljive podatke. "
"Na koji način možete podijeliti &eg; kontaktne podatke osoba sa vašim "
"kolegama ali bez otkrivanja njihovih prihoda? To je moguće ukoliko "
"podijelite samo upit a ne kompletnu tabelu."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1712
#, no-c-format
msgid "Performance and capacity"
msgstr "Performanse i kapacitet"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1713
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Your computer is probably quite fast, however you will easily see that it "
"doesn't help with slow, large spreadsheets. Their low efficiency is first of "
"all due to lack of indexes accelerating the process of data search "
"(databases do offer them). Moreover if you use things like system clipboard, "
"even copying data may become troublesome with time."
msgstr ""
"Vaš računar je vjerovatno veoma brz, međutim uvidjet ćete da vam nije od "
"koristi kada su u pitanju veliki i spori tabelarni prikazi. Njihova niska "
"učinkovitost je prvenstveno zbog nedostatka indeksa koji ubrzavaju proces "
"pretrage podataka(baze podataka nude ove indekse). Dalje, ukoliko koristite "
"stavke poput sistemskog spremnika, nakon nekog vremena čak i kopiranje "
"podataka može postati problematično."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1715
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Spreadsheets containing large data sets may take ages to open. A spreadsheet "
"loads lots of data to the computer's memory while opening. Most of the data "
"loaded are probably useless/unnecessary for you at the moment. Databases "
"unlike spreadsheets load data from computer storage only when needed."
msgstr ""
"Tabelarni prikazi koji sadrže veliku količinu podataka mogu biti jako spori "
"pri otvaranju. Tabelarni prikaz mnogo puni računarsku memoriju prilikom "
"otvaranja sadržaja. Većina podataka su vjerovatno beskorisni/nepotrebni za "
"vas u tom trenutku. Baze podataka, za razliku od tabelarnih prikaza pune "
"podatke u računarsku memoriju samo po potrebi."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1717
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In most cases you will not have to worry how the database stores its data. "
"This means that unlike spreadsheets, databases do not care about:"
msgstr ""
"U većini slučajeva nećete morati brinuti o tome kako baza podataka snima "
"podatke. Ovo znači da za razliku od tabelarnog prikaza, baze podataka ne "
"mare o sljedećem:"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1720
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The sequence of rows since you can order the rows according to your needs. "
"Moreover, you can view the same data in many views with different orders."
msgstr ""
"Redoslijedu redova jer svakako možete premještati redove po potrebi. Čak "
"štaviše, možete gledati isti podatak na mnogo načina prikazivanja sa "
"različitim redoslijedom."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1721
#, no-c-format
msgid "The same goes for columns (fields) of the table."
msgstr "Isto važi i za kolone (polja) tabele."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1723
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Together with <link linkend=\"limiting-data-view\">Limiting data view</link> "
"described in the previous paragraph these qualities constitute the advantage "
"of databases."
msgstr ""
"Zajedno sa <link linkend=\"limiting-data-view\">Ograničavanje prikaza "
"podataka</link> opisanog u prethodnom paragrafu ove osobine čine prednost "
"baza podataka."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1726
#, no-c-format
msgid "Data entry"
msgstr "Unos podataka"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1727
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The latest editions of applications for creating spreadsheets enable you to "
"design data-entry forms. Such forms are most useful if your data cannot be "
"conveniently displayed in tabular view, &eg; if the text occupies too many "
"rows or if all the columns do not fit on the screen."
msgstr ""
"Zadnje verzije aplikacija za kreiranje tabelarnog prikaza omogućavaju vam da "
"dizajnirate obrasce za uos podataka. Takvi obrasci su najkorisniji u slučaju "
"kada se podaci ne mogu prikladno prikazati u tabelarnom prikazu, &eg; "
"ukoliko tekst zauzima previše redova ili ukoliko sve kolone ne mogu stati na "
"ekran."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1729
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this case the very way the spreadsheet works is problematic. Fields for "
"data entry are placed loosely within the spreadsheet and very often are not "
"secure against the user's (intentional or accidental) intervention."
msgstr ""
"U ovom slučaju način rada tabelarnog prikaza je jako problematičan. Polja za "
"unos podataka su slabo postavljena unutar tabelarnih prikaza i veoma često "
"nisu sigurna od korisnikove (namjerne ili slučajne) intervencije."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1732
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Reports</title>"
msgstr "<title>Izvještaji</title>"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1733
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Databases enable grouping, limiting and summing up data in a form of a "
"report. Spreadsheets are usually printed in a form of small tables without "
"fully automatic control over page divisions and the layout of fields."
msgstr ""
"Baze podataka omogućavaju grupisanje, ograničavanje i sumiranje podataka u "
"vidu izvještaja. Tabelarni prikazi su većinom printani u vidu malih tabela "
"bez automatske kontrole izgleda i rasporeda polja."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1736
#, no-c-format
msgid "Programming"
msgstr "Programiranje"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1737
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Applications for creating databases often contain full programming "
"languages. Newer spreadsheets have this capability too, however calculations "
"come down to modifying the spreadsheet's fields and simple data copying, "
"regardless of the relevance and integrity rules mentioned in previous "
"paragraphs."
msgstr ""
"Aplikacije za kreiranje baza podataka često sadrže kompletan programski "
"jezik. Noviji tabelarni prikazi također imaju ovu opciju, međutim proračuni "
"se svode na modificiranje polja tabelarnog prikaza i jednostavno kopiranje "
"podataka, bez obzira na pravila relevantnosti i integriteta koja su "
"spomenuta u prethodnim poglavljima."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1739
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Data processing within a spreadsheet is usually done via a graphical user's "
"interface which may slow down the data processing speed. Databases are "
"capable of working in background, outside of graphical interfaces."
msgstr ""
"Procesiranje podataka u tabelarnom prikazu se najčešće obavlja kroz grafički "
"korisnički interfejs što može usporiti brzinu prenosa podataka. Baze "
"podataka su u mogućnosti da rade u pozadini, bez grafičkog okruženja."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1742
#, no-c-format
msgid "Multiuse"
msgstr "Višenamjenski"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1743
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is hard to imagine a multiuse of one spreadsheet. Even if it is "
"technically possible in the case of the latest applications, it requires a "
"lot of discipline, attention and knowledge from the users, and these cannot "
"be guaranteed."
msgstr ""
"Teško je zamisliti više namjena za jedan tabelarni prikaz. Čak i ukoliko je "
"tehnički izvodivo u slučaju da se radi o najnovijim aplikacijama, to "
"zahtjeva mnogo discipline, pažnje i znanja korisnika što ne može biti "
"garantovano."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1745
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A classical way to sharing data saved in a spreadsheet with other person is "
"to send a file as a whole (usually using e-mail) or providing a spreadsheet "
"file in a computer network. This way of work is ineffective for larger "
"groups of people - data that could be needed in a particular time may be "
"currently locked by another person."
msgstr ""
"Klasični način dijeljenja podataka sa osobama, sačuvan u tabelarnim "
"prikazima jeste da se pošalje datoteka u cjelini(najčešće putem elektronske "
"pošte) ili postavljanjem datoteke na ručunarsku mrežu. Ovaj način rada je "
"neefikasan za veće grupe ljudi - podaci koji su možda potrebni u određenom "
"vremenu su zaključani od strane neke druge osobe."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1747
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the other hand, databases have been designed mainly with multiuser access "
"in mind. Even for the simplest version locking at a particular table row's "
"level is possible, which enables easy sharing of table data."
msgstr ""
"S druge strane, baze podataka su uglavnom dizajnirane za više korisnika. Čak "
"i za najjednostavnije verzije zaključavanja određenog reda tabele je moguće, "
"što omogućava veoma jednostavno dijeljenje tabele podataka."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1750
#, no-c-format
msgid "Security"
msgstr "Sigurnost"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1751
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Securing a spreadsheet or its particular sections with a password is only "
"symbolic activity. After providing a spreadsheet file in a computer network, "
"every person being able to copy the file can try to break the password. It "
"is sometimes not so hard as the password is stored in the same file as the "
"spreadsheet."
msgstr ""
"Osiguravanje tabelarnog prikaza ili neke određene sekcije sa šifrom je samo "
"simbolična radnja. Nakon postavljanja datoteke tabelarnog prikaza na "
"računarsku mrežu, svaka osoba koja je u mogućnosti da kopira datoteku može "
"pokušati provaliti šifru. Ponekad to i nije tako teško jer se šifra čuva u "
"istoj datoteci kao i sam tabelarni prikaz."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1753
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Features for edit locking or copy locking of a spreadsheet (or its part) is "
"equally easy to break."
msgstr ""
"Karakteristike za uređivanje zaključavanjem ili kopiranje zaključavanjem  "
"tabelarnog prikaza(ili njegovog dijela) je jednako lahko za provaliti."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1755
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Databases (except these saved in a file instead of a server) do not need to "
"be available in a single file. You're accessing them using a computer "
"network, usually by providing a user name and a password. You are gaining "
"access only to these areas (tables, forms or even selected rows and columns) "
"which were assigned to you by setting appropriate access rights."
msgstr ""
"Baze podataka(osim onih snimljenih u datoteci umjesto serveru) ne trebaju "
"biti dostupne u jednoj datoteci. Pristupate im koristeći računarsku mrežu, "
"obično sa korisničkim imenom i šifrom. Dobijate pristup samo onim "
"dijelovima(tabele, obrasci ili čak selektirani redovi i kolone) koje su vam "
"dodijeljene u odnosu na postavljena prava pristupa."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1757
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Access rights can affect ability of data editing or only data reading. If "
"any data is not available to you, it will not be even sent to your computer, "
"so there is no possibility of making a copy of the data in such easy way as "
"in case of spreadsheet files."
msgstr ""
"Prava pristupa mogu uticati na mogućnost uređivanja ili samo čitanja "
"podataka. Ukoliko vam bilo koji podatak nije dostupan, neće se čak poslati "
"ni na vaš računar, tako da nema mogućnosti kopiranja istog na način kao u "
"tabelarnom prikazu."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1761
#, no-c-format
msgid "Database Design"
msgstr "Dizajn baze podataka"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1762
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Database design needs careful planning. Note that <replaceable>Persons</"
"replaceable> table redesign proposed in section <link linkend=\"data-"
"integrity-and-validity\">Data integrity and validity</link> can generate "
"problems when the table is filled with data. For example, renaming a field "
"is a simple task, but splitting the <replaceable>Address</replaceable> field "
"into separate fields requires careful and tedious work."
msgstr ""
"Dizajn baze podataka se treba pažljivo isplanirati. Imajte na umu da "
"redizajniranje tabele <replaceable>Osobe</replaceable> u sekciji <link "
"linkend=\"data-integrity-and-validity\">Integritet i validnost podataka</"
"link> može uzrokovati probleme kada je tabela popunjena podacima. Na "
"primjer, preimenovanje polja je jednostavan zadatak, ali podjela polja "
"<replaceable>Adresa</replaceable> u odvojena polja zahtjeva pažnju i dosadan "
"posao."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1764
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To avoid such situations, rethink your database project before you create it "
"in your computer, and before you and others will start to use it. Thus, by "
"investing some time initially, you will most probably save your time on "
"everyday use."
msgstr ""
"Da bi izbjegli takve situacije, razmislite opet o vašem projektu prije nego "
"kreirate bazu podataka i prije nego je vi ili neko drugi počne koristiti. "
"Ukoliko uložite neko vrijeme u razmatranje, vjerovatno ćete uštedjeti na "
"vremenu u svakodnevnom korištenju."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1767
#, no-c-format
msgid "Who Needs a Database?"
msgstr "Kome treba baza podataka?"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1768
#, no-c-format
msgid "Stick to spreadsheets if:"
msgstr "Držite se tabelarnih prikaza ukoliko:"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1770
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Your needs are limited and your data will never grow to large volumes (can "
"you actually forecast that now?)"
msgstr ""
"Ako su vaši zahtjevi ograničeni i podaci nikada neće dostići veliku obimnost "
"(da li to zaista možete predvidjeti sada?)"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1771
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You are unable to acquire the methodology of database construction. You may "
"however consider either outsourcing this task to someone else or using "
"simpler tools."
msgstr ""
"Ako niste u mogućnosti izdizajnirati bazu podataka. U tom slučaju možete "
"bilo proslijediti ovaj zadatak nekom drugom ili koristiti jednostavnij alate."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1772
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You use complicated spreadsheets and you lack time or money to switch to "
"databases. Think or ask someone whether this does not lead down a blind "
"alley. Don't count on magical tools that would change your spreadsheet "
"(regardless how well made) into a database."
msgstr ""
"Ako koristite komplicirane tabelarne prikaze i nemate novca za prelaz na "
"baze podataka. Razmislite o ovome ili se raspitajte prije nego vas ovo "
"odvede u slijepu ulicu. Ne računajte na magične alate koji bi promijenili "
"tabelarne prikaze(bez obzira kako kvalitetno napravljeni) u bazu podataka."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1775
#, no-c-format
msgid "Consider using databases if:"
msgstr "Razmislite o korištenju baze podataka ukoliko:"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1777
#, no-c-format
msgid "Your data collection expands every week."
msgstr "Ako se vaša kolekcija podataka proširuje svake sedmice."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1778
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You often create new spreadsheets, copy within these and you feel that this "
"work is getting more and more tedious. In this case the effort of switching "
"to databases easily pays off."
msgstr ""
"Ako veoma često pravite nove tabelarne prikaze, kopirate iste i osjećate da "
"posao postaje sve više i više dosadan. U ovom slučaju napor pri prelasku na "
"bazu podataka se svakako isplati."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1779
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You create reports and statements for which the table view of a spreadsheet "
"is not suitable. You can then consider switch to using a database with form "
"views."
msgstr ""
"Ako pravite izvještaje i statistike za koje tabelarni prikaz nije prikladan. "
"Tada možete razmotriti opciju korištenja baza podataka sa prikazima u vidu "
"obrasca."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1783
#, no-c-format
msgid "Database Creation Software"
msgstr "Softver za kreiranje baza podataka"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1784
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"So far you have learnt the general characteristics of databases without "
"going into much detail about specific applications for designing them."
msgstr ""
"Do sada ste naučili općenito o osobinama baza podataka bez zalaženja dublje "
"u detalje o konkretnim aplikacijama dizajniranim za njih."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1786
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first databases were built together with large mainframe computers in "
"the 60s, &eg; IBM System/360. Those were not the days of PCs, therefore "
"these databases required a highly specialized personnel. Although the old "
"computers' hardware was unreliable, they were immeasurably slower and had "
"less storage capacity, one feature of databases still remains most "
"attractive: the data access by many users through a network."
msgstr ""
"Prve baze podataka su stvorene zajedno sa velikim računarima 60ih godina, "
"&eg; IBM System/360. To nisu bili dani personalnih računara, stoga baze "
"podataka su zahtijevale visoko kvalificirano osoblje. Iako stari računari "
"nisu bili pouzdani, imali su veoma spor odziv i ne mnogo prostora, jedna "
"karakteristika baza podataka još uvijek ostaje najprivlačnija: pristup "
"podacima za mnogo korisnika putem mreže."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1788
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the 70s scientists formed the theory of relational databases (terms like: "
"table, record, column (field) and relationality and many others). On the "
"basis of this theory IBM DB2 and Oracle databases were created, which have "
"been developed and used till today. In the late 70s the first PCs were "
"constructed. Their users could (gradually) utilize many types of "
"applications, including those for database construction."
msgstr ""
"70ih godina naučnici su oformili teoriju relacionih baza podataka(fraze "
"poput: tabela, zapis, kolona(polja) i mnoge druge). Bazirano na ovoj teoriji "
"IBM DB2 i Oracle baze podataka su napravljene, koje se razvijaju  i dan "
"danas. Kasnih 70ih godina, napravljeni su prvi personalni računari. Njihovi "
"korisnici(postepeno) su upotrebljavali razne tipove aplikacija, uključujući "
"i aplikacije za konstrukciju baze podataka."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1790
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When it comes to large databases in companies, the situation hasn't changed: "
"they still require powerful computers or computer complexes called clusters. "
"This goes, however, beyond the topic of this manual."
msgstr ""
"Kada je riječ o velikim bazama podataka unutar kompanija, situacija se nije "
"promijenila, još uvijek zahtjevaju jake računare ili komplekse računara "
"zvane klasteri. Međutim ovo prevazilazi okvire ovog priručnika."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1792
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the area of <quote>accessible</quote> databases with graphic user "
"interface for PCs you can choose from the following:"
msgstr ""
"U području <quote>dostupnih</quote> baza podataka sa korisničkim interfejsom "
"za personalne računare možete odabrati sljedeće:"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1795
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<ulink url=\"http://www.dbase.com\">DBase</ulink> - a tool for databases "
"operation for DOS popular in the 80s. Files in DBase format are still used "
"in some specific cases due to their simplicity."
msgstr ""
"<ulink url=\"http://www.dbase.com\">DBase</ulink> - alat za operacije nad "
"bazama podataka za DOS, popularan 80ih godina. Datoteke u DBase formatu se i "
"danas koriste, zbog njihove jednostavnosti,  u nekim specijalnim slučajevima."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1796
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<ulink url=\"http://msdn.microsoft.com/vfoxpro/\">FoxPro</ulink> - an "
"application similar to DBase (early 90s). After being taken over by "
"Microsoft, graphic user interfaces were introduced and therefore it is used "
"for creating databases on PCs. This product is still offered, though seems a "
"bit obsolete."
msgstr ""
"<ulink url=\"http://msdn.microsoft.com/vfoxpro/\">FoxPro</ulink> je "
"aplikacija slična DBase (rane 90e). Nakon što je preuzeta od strane "
"Microsofta, počinje se nuditi sa grafičkim korisničkim interfejsom i zbog "
"tog se koristila za kreiranje baza podataka na personalnim računarima. Još "
"uvijek je u ponudi, iako malo zastarjela."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1797
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<ulink url=\"http://office.microsoft.com/access/\">Microsoft Access</ulink> "
"- an application for databases (data and graphic interface design) with many "
"simplifications, therefore suitable for beginners, designed in the late 80s, "
"based on 16-Bit Architecture. This product is offered and widely used till "
"today, especially by small companies, where efficiency and multiuser "
"requirements are not very demanding."
msgstr ""
"<ulink url=\"http://office.microsoft.com/access/\">Microsoft Access</ulink> "
"- aplikacija za baze podataka(podatkovni i grafički dizajn) sa mnogo "
"pojednostavljenja, stoga pogodna za početnike, dizajnirana kasnih 80ih, "
"bazirana na 16bitnoj arhitekturi. Još uvijek je u ponudi i veoma je "
"rasprostranjena, pogotovo unutar malih firmi gdje efikasnost i "
"višekorisnički zahtjevi nisu primarni zahtjevi."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1798
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<ulink url=\"http://www.filemaker.com\">FileMaker</ulink> - popular "
"application similar to MS Access in simplicity, operating on Windows and "
"Macintosh platforms, offered since 1985."
msgstr ""
"<ulink url=\"http://www.filemaker.com\">FileMaker</ulink> - popularna "
"aplikacija, po jednostavnosti slična MS Accessu, upotrebljiva na Windows i "
"Machintosh platformama, u ponudi od 1985."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1799
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<ulink url=\"http://www.calligra-suite.org/kexi\">Kexi</ulink> - a "
"multiplatform application (&UNIX;/&Linux;, Windows, &MacOS; X) designed in "
"2003, developed according to OpenSource principles, part of the global KDE "
"community, that among other things provide a graphic environment for &UNIX;/"
"&Linux; systems. A significant contributor to Kexi's development is the "
"OpenOffice Poland company."
msgstr ""
"<ulink url=\"http://www.calligra-suite.org/kexi\">Kexi</ulink> - aplikacija "
"podržana na više platformi  (&UNIX;/&Linux;, Windows, &MacOS; X), "
"dizajnirana 2003, razvijena po open source principima, dio KDE zajedništva "
"koja između mnoštva drugih stvari nudi grafičko okruženje za  &UNIX;/&Linux; "
"sisteme. Značajan saradnik razvoja Kexija je OpenOffice, Poljska kompanija."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1803
#, no-c-format
msgid "Appendix B. Comparing Kexi to other database applications"
msgstr "Dodatak B. Usporedba Kexi u odnosu na ostale aplikacije baza podataka"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1805
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"data-types\">Data types</link>&nbsp;"
msgstr "<link linkend=\"data-types\">Tipovi podataka</link>&nbsp;"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1807
#, no-c-format
msgid "Data types"
msgstr "Tipovi podataka"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1808
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Although different database applications tend to provide similar "
"functionality, they often use different terminology. For your convenience, "
"this appendix shows how the terminology used in &kexi; corresponds to that "
"used by other database applications. Thus, this chapter may be useful when "
"migrating databases from one application to another."
msgstr ""
"Iako su drukčije aplikacije za baze podataka sklone ponudi istih "
"funkcionalnosti, veoma često koriste drugu terminologiju. Radi vas, ovaj "
"dodatak pokazuje kako terminologija korištena u &kexi; odgovara drugim, "
"korištenim u ostalim aplikacijama baza podataka. Tako da ovo poglavlje može "
"biti veoma korisno pri prenosu baza podataka iz jedne aplikacije u drugu."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1810
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The table below shows how the data types in &kexi; correspond to data types "
"in other database applications."
msgstr ""
"Tabela ispod pokazuje kako tipovi podataka u &kexi; odgovaraju tipovima "
"podataka u drugim aplikacijama."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1812
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some of the data types listed here are sub-types of other types. For "
"example, the <guilabel>Long text</guilabel> type is a sub-type of the "
"<guilabel>Text</guilabel> type. To use a sub-type in &kexi;, you should "
"select the corresponding basic type (in this case, <guilabel>Text</"
"guilabel>) in the table designer, and then select the sub-type using the "
"<guilabel>Subtype</guilabel> setting in the <guilabel>Property Editor</"
"guilabel>."
msgstr ""
"Neki od tipova podataka ovdje su podtipovi od drugih tipova. Na primjer,  "
"tip <guilabel>Dugi tekst</guilabel> je podtip tipa <guilabel>Tekst</"
"guilabel>. Da biste koristili podtip u &kexi; trebali biste selektovati "
"odgovarajući osnovni tip (u ovom slučaju <guilabel>Tekst</guilabel>) u "
"dizajneru tabele, a nakon toga odabrati podtip koristeći <guilabel>Podtip</"
"guilabel> opcije u <guilabel>Uređivaču osobina</guilabel>."

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:1816
#, no-c-format
msgid "Comparison of data types used in Kexi and other database applications"
msgstr ""
